# A name is called on five lost functions; only behind that call does one of them reach code that nobody sees, which lays the prototype of lists above it. The rule of the call opened with a question that nobody watched (has the family reached unseen code?): run once more over the solved sets it took the other road and added something: under the checking word FlowFixpoint the build stopped by name (FlowEndedTooEarly). The question is gone: what unseen code may lay on or above an escaped function arrives at the pool's node and is called there.
# OPTIONS: check=FlowFixpoint
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: FlowEndedTooEarly
# CHECK: function f1 
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: TypeError,TypeError,TypeError,TypeError,TypeError,-,TypeError,TypeError,TypeError,TypeError, b3
